'' Using interface values (docs/tiko-interfaces §5.5, §7.8, §13.2): trycast and 'is' are
'' typed and judged, with the static answer for a type with no vptr (TKO1016); '=' takes a
'' reference of the family or nullptr; 'new' (TKO1007), 'delete' (TKO1013), a temporary
'' (TKO1012), a name two bases declare (TKO1010), a foreign declaration (TKO1015) and
'' differing defaults (TKO1018) are diagnosed. A type-qualified call is the existing
'' TKO0999. trycast and 'is' are TKO0992 until Phase 4; the comparison (51) and nullptr (45)
'' compile.
